\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Training with position error, and adding a second lane cue.} The proposed model reads the road from a map drawn into its input, so it needs to know where the car is on the map. Here the position estimate is shifted by a constant lateral distance (horizontal axis, metres; a small heading error grows with it). Success over 40 episodes for the proposed model and four models trained with random position errors; bands are 95\% intervals. Dashed lines: the map is the only source of lane position. Solid green and pink lines: a second, independent and noisy lane measurement (lateral offset and heading) is also given to the model. 40 episodes per point.}}{44}{figure.caption.36}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:posetrained}{{14}{44}{\textbf {Training with position error, and adding a second lane cue.} The proposed model reads the road from a map drawn into its input, so it needs to know where the car is on the map. Here the position estimate is shifted by a constant lateral distance (horizontal axis, metres; a small heading error grows with it). Success over 40 episodes for the proposed model and four models trained with random position errors; bands are 95\% intervals. Dashed lines: the map is the only source of lane position. Solid green and pink lines: a second, independent and noisy lane measurement (lateral offset and heading) is also given to the model. 40 episodes per point}{figure.caption.36}{}}
